.TH KIRO-XLIBRE-SWAP 8 "2026-07-03" "Kiro" "Kiro System Tools"
.SH NAME
kiro-xlibre-swap \- swap between Xorg and XLibre via the official x11libre.net pacman repo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiro-xlibre-swap
[\fB1\fR|\fB\-\-xlibre\fR]
[\fB2\fR|\fB\-\-rollback\fR]
[\fB3\fR|\fB\-\-status\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiro-xlibre-swap
switches the running system between the stock
.B xorg-server
and
.BR XLibre ,
a drop-in fork of X.Org (\fIhttps://xlibre.net\fR), by adding x11libre.net's
official signed
.B [xlibre]
pacman repository and installing
.B xlibre-xserver
plus
.B xlibre-input-libinput
and a matching
.I xlibre-*
package for every currently installed
.I xf86-*
driver.
.PP
Run with no arguments to get an interactive menu; pass
.B 1
or
.B --xlibre
to install XLibre directly,
.B 2
or
.B --rollback
to reverse the swap and restore Xorg, or
.B 3
or
.B --status
to just report which X server is currently installed without changing
anything.
.PP
Options 1 and 2 must be run as root (the script re-execs itself via
.B sudo
or a graphical polkit prompt when not already root); option 3 does not
require root.
.PP
The AUR
.I xlibre-*-bin
packages are a stale third-party wrapper pinned to abandoned version
numbers that 404 against x11libre.net's current repo layout \(em installing
from the official pacman repo directly, as this script does, is the method
XLibre's own maintainer documents and avoids that breakage entirely.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR 1 ", " \-\-xlibre
Install XLibre: back up the current package list, add the
.B [xlibre]
repo, install
.B xlibre-xserver
and matching drivers, replacing
.B xorg-server
and its
.I xf86-*
drivers. Then reports which X server is now installed.
.TP
.BR 2 ", " \-\-rollback
Restore Xorg: reinstall
.B xorg-server
and matching
.I xf86-*
drivers, then remove the
.B [xlibre]
repo entry from
.IR /etc/pacman.conf .
Then reports which X server is now installed.
.TP
.BR 3 ", " \-\-status
Report which X server is currently installed, via
.B "pacman -Qo /usr/lib/Xorg"
(which package owns the server binary) and
.B "/usr/lib/Xorg -version"
(the banner the binary itself reports). Makes no changes.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without making any changes to
the system. Still shows the interactive menu and confirmation prompt,
but skips them non-interactively when combined with a numeric/flag
choice.
.SH DANGER
This script replaces the system's display server. A failed or partial
swap can leave the system without a graphical session. Before running
option 1 or 2, know how to reach a TTY
.RI ( Ctrl+Alt+F2 )
and log in there. Both options require confirmation at an interactive
prompt before making any change.
.PP
Proprietary GPU drivers (e.g.
.BR nvidia-utils )
may need an
.B IgnoreABI
workaround in
.IR /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d/xlibre.conf ;
see the warning the script prints when
.B nvidia-utils
is detected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Swap, rollback, or status check completed (or simulated in dry-run mode),
or help/version was printed.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown or invalid option/choice was supplied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/kiro-common.sh
Shared library providing logging, colour output, root escalation, and
.B execute_or_dryrun
support.
.TP
.I /var/log/kiro-xlibre-swap-packages.txt
Snapshot of
.B pacman -Qe
taken before installing XLibre.
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.conf.pre-xlibre.bak
Backup of
.I /etc/pacman.conf
taken before the
.B [xlibre]
repo entry is added; removed again on rollback.
.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive menu:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo kiro-xlibre-swap
.EE
.RE
.PP
Install XLibre without the menu:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo kiro-xlibre-swap --xlibre
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check which X server is active:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
kiro-xlibre-swap --status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Roll back to Xorg:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo kiro-xlibre-swap --rollback
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR pacman-key (8),
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR Xorg (1)
